import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 639 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 640 | 2026-10-24 | **Pitch build C (her 00:17 notes: lesson 5 'should be taught on the scale, the keys-between version confused me too'; the group 1 2 3 next to lesson numbers is confusing; everything old the Home does not use will be deleted, so the whole Home must hold it all, books and workbook rebuilt after).** (1) Intervals lesson 5 is now 'Minor: a half step lower' (단음정: 반음 낮게): think of the major scale on the lower note, numbered 1-8 on the keys; a top note in the scale makes a major interval, a half step below a scale note (blue, labelled m3 / 단3) makes it minor; steps: the scale on the lower note, a half step lower (C-E, C-E♭), 6ths 7ths 2nds, from any note (F-E♭), 4ths 5ths octaves stay perfect; questions: major or minor with the scale shown, name it, make it minor; wrong answers explain with the scale ('In the F major scale, note 7 is E. E♭ is a half step lower: a minor 7th.'). Hearing and Turn it upside down answers use the same scale picture (no more counts like 9 or 11); keys-between stays only in lesson 3 (3rds) and Chords. (2) Home groups: an outlined pill with the lesson range (1–2, 3–5, ...) replaces the second set of 1 2 3 circles; lessons keep the filled circles. (3) Keys and staff, Korean: the English mnemonics (Every Good Boy..., Great Big Dragon..., All Cows Eat Grass) left the Korean lines; letters only. (4) Inventory of what lives only in old chapters / toolbox / books, per area, started for the move to the Home. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch662.py,kq.jsx,iv.jsx,ch.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
